INT. TAXIDERMY WORKSHOP - DAY

Glass eyes in trays. A stuffed heron. Dust in the skylight.

INSPECTOR NELL BARROWMAN (40s, notebook) circles a workbench. Beside her, CONSTABLE JUNO ADEYEMI (20s) scribbles.

Behind the counter, MARGUERITE HOLLIS (60s, leather apron) polishes a badger.

At the back, ALFRED PETTIGREW (70s, cardigan) sits very still. A suspect, or furniture.

MARGUERITE
Nobody touched the owl.

NELL
Somebody did. The base is cracked.

ALFRED
It was always cracked.

JUNO
Sir, the report says --

NELL
Juno. Later.

MARGUERITE
She dropped it in March, Alfred.

ALFRED
She did not. She said she did.

NELL
Who is "she" now?

MARGUERITE
(over Nell)
Her. The girl from the post office.

ALFRED
(over Marguerite)
Nobody. There's no girl.

JUNO
She told me there was a ledger.

Nell lifts the heron's wing. A key glints in the feathers.
